Steps:
1. Tap Show — the window starts at the bottom right (BOTTOM_END);
2. Tap Grow / Shrink a few times (the buttons inside the card work too);
3. Expected: the bottom-right corner never moves and the card only grows towards the top left — 2.x drifted further off screen every time.

Steps:
1. Tap Show the Compose window, then tap the window a few times to raise count / vm;
2. Open the second page or the blacklisted page, or rotate the screen;
3. Expected: the window stays (except on the blacklisted page, where the config asks it to disappear), count and vm keep their values when you return, and the window never turns blank or crashes.

The three filter styles on AppHost.Builder:
· blacklist(Class...) / whitelist(Class...): subclasses included;
· blacklist(String...) / whitelist(String...): exact fully qualified names;
· filter { activity -> ... }: any rule you like (by package, by Intent extras, …), callable several times, all of them must pass.

Steps:
1. Tap Show, then Allow bottom overflow and turn adsorption off (otherwise it snaps back to an edge);
2. Drag the window to the very bottom, over the navigation bar;
3. Expected: the content stays fully visible, is never cut in half, and stays put after you let go.

Steps:
1. Tap the button below to add the Fragment;
2. ScopeFragment calls fxScope("scope-frag").show() in onCreate, before it has a root view;
3. Expected: as soon as the Fragment view is created the Frag window shows up inside the grey area below, and it can only be dragged inside that area.
